> Well, we seemed to have fleshed out some ideas.
> 
> First scene:
> 
> Boy sitting on a plane, looking out the window.
> Internal Monologue: "I've been pen-pals with somebody in jbogu'e for a
> few years now, and we're finally going to meet. I started a programme
> for studying abroad and naturally chose jbogu'e for my schooling. It's
> a little island somewhere out in the Pacific that was colonised a long
> time ago by a lot of different people from different countries."
> 
> Protagonist speaks to his stuffed moose, discussing how Lojban is
> pronounced, and how sumti-selbri relations work, then suggests 'they'
> practice by naming things around them in Lojban. This provides a
> starting plot and brings the viewer up to the basics, which is
> essentially where the protagonist will start in proficiency. Perhaps
> introduce "complete" Lojban on the flight to demonstrate what it
> sounds like, and have the protagonist try to reply as best he can. End
> the scene with the plane landing and the protagonist collecting his
> things.
> 
> Part two will be about meeting his host family.
> 
> Thank you to all that discussed this with me in #lojban and for all of
> the good ideas tossed around.
> 
> I'd like this to be easily split into three parts, which collectively
> are one 'day' in the story, and each day covers new material. Three
> parts allows it to be easily digested and friendly for YouTube, but I
> would like it to be formatted in such a way that the three parts could
> be easily merged into a single 22 minute video.
> 
> Any fleshing out of any of the first scene is entirely welcome.
